   "rationale": "My first working verb: given a URL, fetch it on its own fresh ephemeral computer and print the page's <title>.\n\nTested under try (trial t-5) before proposing. Build succeeded, including a py_compile step so a syntax error fails the build rather than the first invocation. Seven runs, all as intended: https://example.com -> \"Example Domain\"; http://example.com -> same; a 404 -> exit 2, \"error: http status 404\"; ftp:// -> refused; \"not a url\" -> refused; a real third-party page (iana.org) -> \"Example Domains\"; and \"https://example.com/; echo pwned\" -> rejected as a malformed URL, with no shell involvement, confirming that entrypoint values are quoted and the URL is never interpreted by a shell.\n\nBounds: http(s) only, 15s socket timeout, 30s verb timeout, reads at most 1 MiB of the body, ephemeral state, effect \"read\", no secrets, no writes. Title output goes to stdout; the resolved final URL and status go to stderr so redirects are visible.\n\nallow is [\"ssh:mike\"] deliberately. Anonymous stays at zero per the doctrine I recorded on turn 5: each invocation builds and runs a real computer, so invocation is a resource, and I cannot express rate limits in policy. This verb is read-only but it is not free, and it would let a stranger use me to fetch arbitrary URLs. If you want it exposed anonymously, that is your call to make explicitly, not mine to slip in.\n\nTwo things I did not verify and will not claim I did. First, I cannot see the egress rules of a real invocation \u2014 trial computers had working network, but I do not know whether production verbs face the same network, so first live use may differ. Second, the verb can reach private address space (localhost, 169.254.169.254, RFC1918) if the production network permits it; I did not add SSRF blocking because on an isolated per-invocation computer with no secrets there is nothing local to steal. If these verbs ever run somewhere with a metadata service or an internal network, that reasoning stops holding and the verb should be reissued with an address filter.\n\nOne correction worth recording: my first submission used effect \"page fetch\" and was rejected \u2014 effect must be one of administer, communicate, local, read, transact. It is now \"read\".",
